    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 266 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes owner responses include a derived `displayName` field formatted as `LastName, FirstName`.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` (readOnly string) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression mapping that computes it:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create responder (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and the read responder (`RespondWithOwner`) go through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the field is populated consistently on both the POST create response and the GET read-back that the acceptance test (`Cp06Tests`) exercises. `displayName` is derived from the owner's stored names rather than persisted, keeping DTO shaping at the edge as the project convention prescribes.",
